<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/rule/discipline-frame-completeness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Declares that every instance of the annotated class must carry the named reference-frame property (CONSTITUTION P11, frame-relativity gate): 'a value asserted without its frame is ill-formed'. The frame-relativity SHACL shape is GENERATED from this declaration — exactly one frame when the named property is owl:FunctionalProperty, at least one otherwise — so a new frame-relative value class is enforced the moment it is declared, never by remembering to hand-write its shape. Pair with gmeow:ruleSeverity \"advisory\" to downgrade the generated shape from the binding violation to an advisory warning." <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/graph/fanout/catalog/constraint-catalog.nq> .
